{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reversing an inequality reversing an inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md","fileName":"Reversing an Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reversing an Inequality","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Inequalities and Intervals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Number Line","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"reversing an inequality reversing an inequality","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md","fileName":"Reversing an Inequality.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Reversing an Inequality","heading":"Reversing an Inequality","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Reversing an inequality changes (<) to (>) or (\\leq) to (\\geq), and conversely. It is required when both sides are multiplied or divided by a negative number.\n\nFor (-2x\\leq-10), division by (-2) gives (x\\geq5). The reversal occurs because multiplication by a negative reflects ordered points across zero on the [[Number Line]]. Forgetting it produces the opposite solution set. Adding or subtracting a negative number does not itself trigger reversal; the rule concerns multiplication or division by a negative value.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Inequalities and Intervals","Number Line","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Reversing an Inequality.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Reversi